From e5bc592fdbc7133cd446e264fe92ecfd3895c28c Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: caoanhhao <caoanhhao@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Tue, 24 Nov 2026 23:47:25 +0700
Subject: [PATCH 099/107] drm/panel: nt36523: gts7l: stock on-commands as a
 table, backlight on both links

The CSOT PPA957DB1 on-command list of the stock
ss_dsi_panel_NT36523_PPA957DB1_WQXGA node (sleep out included) has some 360
entries. Keep it as a { delay, length, bytes } table and send every entry to
both DSI links, then display on to both. The panel is reset and initialised
on every prepare, and sent display off and sleep in on disable, as for the
other panels of this driver.

With bonded DSI hosts that run synchronised (qcom,sync-dual-dsi), msm only
queues a command sent to DSI0 and transmits it when the same command is sent
to DSI1. The backlight used DSI0 alone, so its brightness never reached the
panel: the stock init sequence sets the brightness to 0 and the panel stayed
dark after a reset. Send the brightness to every link, as the init sequence
does, and read it back from the first link that answers (this panel answers
reads on DSI1 only).

This replaces the gts7l bring-up switches (skip reset/init/disable, init
bisection, DCS read/write module parameters).

caoanhhao used AI to code
